Z||000015||mrfiero||08-23-2001||12:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>  I figure it prob was a Tiptronic in the Ferrari, all she had to do was tap the downshift button a couple times and poof.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Nope......it had to be a regular tranny.  From everything I have read about the F1 models (those with paddle shifters) the  computer that controls things won't allow for downshifts like that.  <P>Sort of like the auto. trannies in our Fieros (and any other car)......you can downshift to L2 or L1 at 100 MPH, but until you reach a certain RPM it won't shift into L2.<P>The Ferrari is a lot more sophisticated than that, so there would be no way she could have blown things up with an F1 tranny.....it had to be a "regular" one.<P><BR>||||reg||1
