Z||000020||Black88GT||08-23-2001||03:58 PM||||I was thinking the same thing Ken.  Also, isn't it funny how dramatic the news story is.  "Britney WRECKS Ferrari" umm a 25k repair bill isn't even a quarter of the Ferrari's worth.  "Wrecking" it would be unrepairable damage or damage exceeding the value of the car.  <P>Anywho, can anyone verify the gearing?<P>Hey I just noticed something.  In the second line it says "blew up the gear box", in the fourth line it says "damage to the motor".  Which is it?  Something isn't right here.  I would imagine either one would cost more then 25 grand to fix.  I am no Ferrari dealer but the car is around 160 grand I think, who wants to buy a 360 Modena with a "rebuilt" motor/tranny?  If I was the rental company I would demand a new motor/tranny and sell the old ones.   <P>Also it says "crashing to a stop" so if she did "crash" into something thats body work too.  Just doesn't add up.<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 08-23-2001).]||||reg||1
