Z||000029||Pontiaddict||08-24-2001||03:05 AM||||According to Motor Trend, the triptronic is computer controlled and ties into the drive by wire system to control engine speed as well as when the transmission shifts. (in other words, it heel toes for you, among other things) If anyone manages to get it into 2nd at 85 and do damage to the engine or tranny, it would be Ferrari's fault and not due to the mistake of the driver. If a Modena can't do 85 in 2nd it should in 3rd and she could have put it back into 2nd instead of going into 4th.<p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 08-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000030||artherd||08-24-2001||01:20 PM||||This dosen't add up.<P>First, it's NOT a bloody tiptronic! that's a Porsche automatic with buttons. :(<P>Ferrari uses what they call simply "F1" transmission.  Which is a manual 6-speed gearbox with a clutch.  Everything has computer control, and it will shift with blinding speed.<P>It will allow you to bounce off the rev limiter, however it will not allow you to select a gear that would force an over-rev of the engine on downshift (ie first at 120)<P>A 360 is just getting into the powerband at 85mph in 2nd (as grinthock can probally attest :) :)  so an F1 would surely have not only allowed the shift, but blipped and rev-matched in a way that you just have to expierence to belive !!!<P>It is more likely that the car was a standard stick-shift 6-speed, but that dosen't erase the fact that the rear would simply alarmingly break loose if you jammed it.    you've all done this, shift to second while going about 45 or so in a fiero, only don't rev-match...  screebraaAAAWW....  the rear tyres break lose under the engine breaking.<P>This could surely cause someone stupid enough to do this at 85 to lose total control of the car, however it would NOT cause damage to either the engine, or tranny....<P>The repair bill sounds low.  While filming the bond flick "goldeneye" the DB7 actually 'contacted' the rear bumper/quarterpannel. (read: hit during a stunt, not hard, but hit) the 355tb Ferrari driven by Femke Jensen.  The repair bill was nearly $80,000 for the ferrari.  the DB7 was unharmed.... (the carbon of the ferrari is more brittle :)<P>PS: was she killed in this accident again too? ;0)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000031||Pontiaddict||08-24-2001||03:20 PM||||I used tiptronic becaused that was what was used in the articles I've read about the car. They said it was actually called the F1 as you stated. Tiptronic was used more as a household name for push button shifting than the actual Porsche trademark.<P>As for the fact that the car still wouldn't have been damaged by simply doing what was said in the article, that was the point I was attempting to make.<BR>$25000 does sound kind of low. ||||reg||1
Z||000032||rogergarrison||08-24-2001||05:05 PM||||in the mags Ive read ,'tiptronic' sorta has.<BR>become the generic name for on the wheel buttons to shift. The article was sent to me, and like I said I just heard the same things on a couple of TV shows. I didnt mean to make a federal case out of it. She could have downshifted and ground the gears breaking teeth, etc. and like you said if she did get into too low a gear it would have been like slaming on breaks to someone who dont know what there doing. Ive put cars even into reverse going down freeway, smoking tires and not knowing what the hell was going on for a few seconds. then with it out of control she could have just skidded over a median and into a curb. Being in body repair business Ive seen bills go all kinds of ways. Just yesterday saw a wreck that tore whole front end off a Tempo. The Explorer that hit him broke out left side front lites, bent bumper and fender back. didnt even jam his door or flatten a tire. He drove off after they made out report. I had a guy just hand pushing an escort, run into my Mercedes in a parking lot. do $3,000 worth of damage. It all depends how you hit whatever. So maybe she just needed some transmission internal repairs, wheel and tire, etc. I dont think it was she like ran head on into a tree with it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
